    <string name="help_text">1. Choose the language of the text (left) and the language you want (right).\n\n2. Tap Capture and photograph the text, or pick an image from the gallery.\n\n3. The translated text is drawn over the original, in the same place. Use \"Show original\" to compare.\n\n4. Tap any text block on the image — or the Edit button — to correct the recognized text or the translation.\n\n5. Tap Save to keep the result in History.\n\nTips: fill the frame with the text, hold steady, and avoid glare. The first translation for a new language downloads a small language model; after that everything works offline.</string>
    <string name="terms_text">SnapTranslate is provided \"as is\", without warranty of any kind. Translations are produced automatically by an on-device model and may be inaccurate; do not rely on them for medical, legal or safety-critical decisions.</string>
    <string name="privacy_text">Text recognition and translation run entirely on your device. Your photos, the recognized text and your history never leave the device. The app uses the network only to download translation language models from Google.</string>
    <string name="licenses_text">AndroidX, CameraX and Material Components for Android — Apache License 2.0\n\nGoogle ML Kit (Text Recognition, Translation) — ML Kit Terms of Service\n\nMaterial Icons — Apache License 2.0</string>
